Z||000010||Monkeyman||12-29-1999||11:43 PM||||I scoped out this body about 2 months ago.  It costs 4000 English pounds which is either $2500US or $6000Us (I keep getting the math mixed up.)  It comes with everything but the wheels.  Another one of their bodies is the Fiero SS which is 3995# (the symbol isn't right, but you get my point) and it comes with wheels.  The Fiero Factory said that the F282 is much easier to assemble and the fit and finish is much better, too.  (Do you know how much it costs to call England?!?!?! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)  The shipping to Chicago (closest "hub" to me) would be somewhere around 1300# if memory serves me (but when has it? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
