Z||000018||batboy||12-31-1999||09:16 AM||||I like it, probably way too expensive for my low budget projects though. I wonder what size dash stereo speakers are used? Those can't be 4" X 10" grill covers. Still no cup holder?||||reg||1
Z||000019||Monkeyman||12-31-1999||12:59 PM||||Go to "Is Eddy Snaauw's dash available for purchase?" in this forum.  I posted his web address.  It has some other pics of the dash in various states of undress.  It kinda looks like it might be sized for 3.5s.  (I hope not, although there are some killer 3.5" speakers out there.  Go to Crutchfields site.  Better selection of 3.5s than 4x10s!)  IMHO, 3.5" speakers wouldn't be enough for the front, but if you're gonna spend $1500 (?) for a dash, you can probably afford to do some custom work on a stereo, too and add additional speakers.  (Maybe some in the footwells, seats (like '84s and '85s) and sail panels plus a sub or two!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  BTW--You don't really need a cup holder.  That's what the passenger is for. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||TOM||12-31-1999||02:27 PM||||There used to be one one rebody I would ever consider. No there is two. But Im not too fond off that dash. To each there own.||||reg||1
Z||000021||batboy||12-31-1999||02:30 PM||||I admit, there are nice 3.5" speakers out there, but they can barely put out any mid-range. They're mainly a tweater. A 4" round speaker is amazingly better sounding than a 3.5" for not being that much bigger. I bet the dash could easily be modified for the 4" speakers.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Shiner||12-31-1999||03:35 PM||||GPS system??!?  Cup holder?!?<BR>These are the kinds of things I HATE about new sports cars (take a look at the Boxster S, for instance) It's all gadgets and whoozits.  An electronic top?  Come one.  GPS nav systems in sports cars, are, IMHO incredibly lame.  Christopher Columbus didn't need directions, and neither do I!  <P> One of the things I like most about the fiero is the simplicity.  Although it is electronicly controlled, it's done so in a manner that is unintrusive.  <P> I guess I am kind of a sports car purist at heart.  3000GT's make me sick to my stomach.  If it was up to me, I would drive a 1965 Shelby Cobra 427 in the summer, and a fiero in the winter!  ||||reg||8
